style='Match the approved Week 1 course reference in silhouette, restrained flat color, and dark navy outlines (#0A4054), with teal (#029990) as the main accent. Use modest natural wood and skin tones where needed. No glossy 3D, neon, glow, decorative gears, drop shadows, embedded labels or full-canvas fill. Export true RGBA transparency. The image is an illustrative teaching analogy, not a screenshot or documented result.'
for c in concepts:
    a=actual[c['n']-1]; s=next(x for x in source['slides'] if x['id']==c['anchor'])
    c.update(title=s['title'], hidden=a['hidden'], current_text=a['text'])
    if c['priority']!='Reuse': c['prompt']+=' '+style
(here/'concepts.json').write_text(json.dumps({'status':'Concept proposals only; no generated assets or deck changes','date':'2026-10-13','source_deck':str(deck.resolve()),'concepts':concepts},indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf8')
esc=lambda s: html.escape(str(s),quote=True)
parts=[]
for c in concepts:
    route='Optional' if c['hidden'] else 'Live'
    badges=''
    if c['priority']=='Reuse':
        badges='<div class="badges">'+''.join(f'<a href="../../../Visuals/Icons/Legacy/week1-{b}.png"><img alt="{b.title()} badge" src="../../../Visuals/Icons/Legacy/week1-{b}.png">{b.title()}</a>' for b in ['constraints','systems','leverage','throughput'])+'</div>'
    fields=''.join(f'<h4>{label}</h4><p>{esc(c[key])}</p>' for key,label in [('edit','Field-level proposal'),('layout','Composition'),('notes','Read-aloud notes'),('rationale','Teaching rationale'),('limit','Limits of the illustration')])
    parts.append(f'''<article id="s{c['n']}" data-route="{route.lower()}" data-priority="{esc(c['priority'])}"><p class="meta">{esc(c['priority'])} · {route} · deck position {c['n']} · printed anchor {c['anchor']}</p><h2>{esc(c['title'])}</h2><div class="compare"><section><h3>Current slide</h3><a href="../PacedDeck20261013/previews/slide-{c['n']:02}.png"><img class="slide" alt="Current slide {c['n']}: {esc(c['title'])}" src="../PacedDeck20261013/previews/slide-{c['n']:02}.png"></a><details><summary>Exact text extracted from the PowerPoint</summary><ul>{''.join('<li>'+esc(t)+'</li>' for t in c['current_text'])}</ul></details></section><section><h3>Proposed concept · {esc(c['name'])}</h3><p class="job">{esc(c['job'])}</p><p>{esc(c['scene'])}</p>{badges}<p class="meta">{'Existing assets shown above.' if badges else 'Written concept only. Image has not been generated.'}</p></section></div>{fields}<details><summary>Ready-to-use generation brief</summary><p>{esc(c['prompt'])}</p><p>Reference: <a href="../../../Visuals/Reference/week1-slide-82.jpg">Week 1 slide 82</a>. Use this for visual continuity; do not copy its four badges into a new illustration.</p></details></article>''')

page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Week 7 · generated imagery concepts</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f7f7fa;color:#201d29;font:17px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1380px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1{font-size:38px;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:28px}h3{font-size:21px}h4{margin-bottom:4px}p{margin-top:6px}a{color:#59429b}header,article,.intro{background:#fff;padding:28px;margin-bottom:28px;border-bottom:2px solid #ddd6eb}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.compare{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:30px}.slide{width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #dedbe5}.job{font-weight:bold;color:#0a4054}.meta{font-size:14px;color:#655e72}.badges{display:flex;gap:12px}.badges a{width:24%;text-align:center;font-size:14px}.badges img{width:100%}details{margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#59429b}input,select{font:inherit;padding:8px;margin:8px}label{display:inline-block}article[hidden]{display:none}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:top}th{background:#f0ebfa}@media(max-width:850px){main{padding:12px}.compare{grid-template-columns:1fr}header,article,.intro{padding:18px}}@media print{input,select,.filters{display:none}article{break-inside:avoid}body{background:white}}</style></head><body><main>
<header><p class="meta">Instructor review · 13 October 2026 · proposal v1</p><h1>Week 7: imagery that carries a teaching point</h1><p>Start with three illustrations: the wrong completed goal, the revised prop in context, and the independent peer attempt. Use each inside an existing slide. The deck already has useful demonstrations, production captures, and process diagrams; these proposals target the conceptual and human moments between them.</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> Brainstorm and generation briefs only. No images generated and no PowerPoint edited.</p><nav><a href="../PacedDeck20261013/output/Week_7_Paced_150_Minutes_v1.pptx">Reviewed paced deck</a><a href="../PacedDeck20261013/index.html">Existing deck review</a><a href="../../../Visuals/Reference/week1-slide-82.jpg">Week 1 visual reference</a><a href="concepts.json" download>Download concept briefs</a></nav><p class="meta">Reviewed all 71 existing slide previews and extracted actual PowerPoint text and hidden-slide flags. The latest local paced output is the baseline. Deck position and printed anchor are both shown because they differ. No new source or research claims are introduced.</p></header>
<section class="intro"><h2>Where generation earns its place</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Placement</th><th>Why this helps</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><a href="#s28">28 · Interface and experience</a></td><td>A visual mismatch makes successful execution versus successful task concrete.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a href="#s30">30 · User stories</a></td><td>An artist inspecting a prop makes the benefit of the tool visible.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a href="#s44">44 · A task another person can attempt</a></td><td>The author’s posture models observation without coaching.</td></tr><tr><td>Reuse</td><td><a href="#s49">49 · Your next revision</a></td><td>The original four lenses reconnect the critique to Week 1.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Maintain the current white/lavender slide treatment. Bring Week 1 continuity through the artwork and familiar meanings rather than changing the deck theme. Keep all labels, questions, and explanatory text editable in PowerPoint.</p><p>Generate one scene per image with a clear silhouette and true transparency. Test the result on the actual slide at presentation size. Exact counts, object continuity, and the intended relationship must survive inspection; a beautiful image that obscures the point should be rejected.</p><h3>Visuals I would keep as evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>7–8 and 11:</strong> actual setup, execution and selection evidence. If more context is needed, capture the real application.</li><li><strong>10, 13 and 18:</strong> precise shared-asset, handoff and backend relationships. Concrete course props or real crops could strengthen them; generated machinery would add ambiguity.</li><li><strong>19–21 and 33–38:</strong> real fixture states, recovery, sample-data UI and implementation excerpts. Enlarge or crop the existing evidence when needed.</li><li><strong>25–26:</strong> preserve the fictional assessment tables and the order of the reveal. An illustration that telegraphs the error could spoil the prediction.</li><li><strong>35 and 40–41:</strong> keep the production examples. Generated game or tool screenshots would weaken their evidentiary value.</li><li><strong>45–48:</strong> preserve the testing roles, timing and rotations. A second decorative scene would compete with procedural instructions.</li></ul><h3>Ideas to skip</h3><p>A Python snake wrapped around Unreal, a generic robot pressing buttons, an iceberg for UX, and a maze for “confusing tools” are recognizable but too detached from this deck’s specific tasks. Likewise, a padlock would overstate tool safety, and a rewind symbol would imply universal Undo.</p></section>
<div class="filters"><label>Search <input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Slide, topic or concept"></label><label>Route <select id="route"><option value="all">All concepts</option><option value="live">Live slides</option><option value="optional">Optional slides</option></select></label><label>Priority <select id="priority"><option value="all">All priorities</option><option>First batch</option><option>Reserve</option><option>Reuse</option></select></label></div>
'''+''.join(parts)+'''<footer><p>New illustrations would be generated teaching analogies. Existing previews and badges remain course assets; this review does not assign new rights or provenance to them. The four badge names and color meanings stay unchanged. Generation would require saving the exact prompt, approved reference, returned original, alpha verification, and final placement in the course visual manifest.</p></footer></main><script>const q=document.querySelector('#search'),r=document.querySelector('#route'),p=document.querySelector('#priority');function filter(){document.querySelectorAll('article').forEach(a=>a.hidden=!(a.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q.value.toLowerCase())&&(r.value==='all'||a.dataset.route===r.value)&&(p.value==='all'||a.dataset.priority===p.value)))}[q,r,p].forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('input',filter));function reveal(){const a=document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));if(a&&a.tagName==='ARTICLE'){q.value='';r.value='all';p.value='all';filter();a.scrollIntoView()}}window.addEventListener('hashchange',reveal);reveal();</script></body></html>'''
